{"_configFromHook":{"title":"Selfhosting With Podman / Ebrahim Haghshenas"},"pageId":"/src/pages/posts/@slug","routeParams":{"slug":"selfhosting-with-podman"},"data":{"post":{"slug":"selfhosting-with-podman","title":"Selfhosting With Podman","subtitle":"Running 20+ services with dinit quadlets.","timestamp":1781678174000,"tags":[{"slug":"podman","name":"Podman"},{"slug":"artix","name":"Artix Linux"}],"image":"!undefined","words":910,"minutes":5,"content":"Babel is an extremely powerful tool for frontend development. Chances are you will\n[find the plugin you need on **npm**](https://www.npmjs.com/search?q=babel%20plugin),\nbut what if you need something novel?\n\n## Use cases\n\n- Adding transformations to personal TypeScript/JavaScript libraries\n- Automating test cases or mocks\n- Simple codemods\n\n## Learn these terms\n\n- [**AST**](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abstract_syntax_tree): Source code abstracted as a JavaScript object. When Babel parses code, it\n  transforms it into this.\n- **Nodes**: These are objects representing specific [Babel types](https://babeljs.io/docs/en/babel-types)\n  in the AST\n- **Paths**: These are objects that link nodes to one another in the AST\n- [**Visitor**](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Visitor_pattern): Visitors\n  allow you to perform operations on specific paths in the AST based on\n  their type\n\n## Treat yourself\n\n- Do yourself a favor and prefer TypeScript to JavaScript when writing your plugin.\n- Type guards (e.g. `t.isObjectProperty(path)`) in `@babel/types` create a flawless autocomplete\n  experience and result in more resilient plugins.\n\n## Libraries you'll need\n\n- [**@babel/core**](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@babel/core): Parse source code into an AST and transform it.\n  In particular, see the `parseAsync()` and `transformAsync()` API references.\n- [**@babel/types**](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@babel/types): Check node types and construct new AST nodes.\n- [**@babel/generator**](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@babel/generator): Generate source code from an AST.\n- [**@babel/template**](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@babel/template): Build an AST from strings and placeholders\n  rather than the utility functions in `@babel/types`.\n- [**@babel/helper-plugin-utils**](https://babeljs.io/docs/en/next/babel-helper-plugin-utils.html): Provide clear messages\n  to your plugin users if their Babel version doesn't have APIs required by your plugin.\n- [**babel-plugin-tester**](https://github.com/babel-utils/babel-plugin-tester): The easiest way to test your babel plugin.\n\n## Resources\n\n- [**Babel Plugin Handbook**](https://github.com/kentcdodds/babel-plugin-handbook/blob/master/README.md#table-of-contents): Go\n  deeper into Babel plugin concepts.\n- [**Babel Types**](https://babeljs.io/docs/en/babel-types): Quickly search for the AST\n  node types you're looking for.\n- [**Babel Plugin Macros**](https://github.com/kentcdodds/babel-plugin-macros): Allow\n  plugin users to utilize your plugin transformations without adding it to their\n  Babel config. This is useful for libraries like [create-react-app](https://github.com/facebook/create-react-app)\n  that don't allow you to customize your plugins.\n\n## Finding examples\n\n- **Hiding in plain sight**: The best place to find example plugins is the [Babel monorepo](https://github.com/babel/babel/tree/eea156b2cb8deecfcf82d52aa1b71ba4995c7d68/packages)\n  itself.\n- **Less is more**: The more basic the plugin, the more fruitful for understanding.\n  - [@babel/plugin-proposal-export-default-from](https://github.com/babel/babel/blob/eea156b2cb8deecfcf82d52aa1b71ba4995c7d68/packages/babel-plugin-proposal-export-default-from/src/index.js)\n  - [@babel/plugin-transform-react-constant-elements](https://github.com/babel/babel/blob/eea156b2cb8deecfcf82d52aa1b71ba4995c7d68/packages/babel-plugin-transform-react-constant-elements/src/index.js)\n  - [@babel/plugin-transform-object-assign](https://github.com/babel/babel/blob/eea156b2cb8deecfcf82d52aa1b71ba4995c7d68/packages/babel-plugin-transform-object-assign/src/index.js)\n  - [@babel/plugin-transform-duplicate-keys](https://github.com/babel/babel/blob/eea156b2cb8deecfcf82d52aa1b71ba4995c7d68/packages/babel-plugin-transform-duplicate-keys/src/index.js)\n\n## Anatomy of a plugin\n\nThis is a contrived example of a Babel plugin that hoists all duplicate `StringLiteral` types to\na higher scope. In the real world more nuanced logic is required to avoid replacing object\nproperty keys and mutable strings willy-nilly.\n\n**What you're going to see**\n\n- Plugin options, state\n- A few built-in plugin utilities\n- What `enter()` and `exit()` visitors look like\n\n```ts title=\"src/utils.ts\"\nimport * as t from \"@babel/types\";\nimport * as babel from \"@babel/core\";\n\nexport default function babelPluginHoistCommonStrings() {\n  return {\n    // This provides the user with better error messages if\n    // our plugin throws\n    name: \"hoist-common-strings\",\n    // And here is the meat of your plugin - the visitor\n    visitor: {\n      /**\n       * @param path This is the Path we talked about above. It\n       *  is an object that links Nodes together.\n       * @param state An object that contains a bunch of metadata\n       *  about the ... state ... of the transformation. Here you'll find:\n       *    - state.ast: The current AST from its root Node\n       *    - state.code: The code string being transformed\n       *    - state.opts: Plugin options\n       *    - state.cwd: The working directory of the user\n       *    - state.filename: The absolute filename of file\n       *      currently being transformed\n       */\n      StringLiteral(path: babel.NodePath\u003ct.StringLiteral>, state: any) {\n        // state.opts give us access to options specific to this plugin\n        // provided by the user with ['hoist-common-strings', {...options...}]\n        const { minLen = 2 } = state.opts;\n\n        // Here we're going to add the paths for each string literal that\n        // was used to our state. This will allow us to count them later\n        // and make sure our `minUses` option was surpassed.\n        const { node } = path;\n        state.commonStrings = state.commonStrings || {};\n        const { commonStrings } = state;\n        // Only hoist strings that surpass our minimum length\n        if (node.value.length >= minLen) {\n          commonStrings[node.value] = commonStrings[node.value] || [];\n          commonStrings[node.value].push(path);\n        }\n      },\n      // Program is at the root of the AST\n      Program: {\n        /**\n         * This is a method on our visitor that is going to be\n         * called right before the visitor exits the node.\n         */\n        exit(path: babel.NodePath\u003ct.Program>, state: any) {\n          // state.opts give us access to options specific to this plugin\n          // provided by the user with ['hoist-common-strings', {...options...}]\n          const { minUses = 1 } = state.opts;\n          // These are the strings we found matching our criteria\n          const { commonStrings } = state;\n\n          for (const string in commonStrings) {\n            const paths = commonStrings[string];\n            // This ensures we only hoist common strings that are used\n            // more than the user's `minUses` option\n            if (paths.length > minUses) {\n              // Babel has some greate utilities that come with\n              // each plugin. To cover them all in one post\n              // would be impossible.\n              //\n              // This helper will create a unique Identifier node\n              // specific to this string\n              const id = path.scope.generateUidIdentifier(string);\n              // Here we replace each of our string paths with the Identifier\n              // returned above\n              paths.forEach((stringPath: babel.NodePath\u003ct.StringLiteral>) => {\n                stringPath.replaceWith(id);\n              });\n              // Finally, we add our Identifier into AST\n              path.scope.push({ id, init: t.stringLiteral(string) });\n            }\n          }\n        },\n      },\n    },\n  };\n}\n```\n\nGiven the input:\n\n```js\nconst MyObject = {\n  hello: \"world\",\n  hello1: \"world\",\n  hello2: \"world\",\n  a: \"a\",\n  a1: \"a\",\n  a2: \"a\",\n};\n```\n\nWe expect the output:\n\n```js\nvar _world = \"world\";\nconst MyObject = {\n  hello: _world,\n  hello1: _world,\n  hello2: _world,\n  a: \"a\",\n  a1: \"a\",\n  a2: \"a\",\n};\n```\n\n[Click here](https://github.com/jaredLunde/babel-plugin-example) to see the plugin and its associated tests on **GitHub**"},"html":"\u003cp>Babel is an extremely powerful tool for frontend development. Chances are you will\n\u003ca href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/search?q=babel%20plugin\">find the plugin you need on \u003cstrong>npm\u003c/strong>\u003c/a>,\nbut what if you need something novel?\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"use-cases\" tabindex=\"-1\">\u003ca class=\"anchor\" href=\"#use-cases\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cspan class=\"anchor-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003c/span>\u003c/a>Use cases\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Adding transformations to personal TypeScript/JavaScript libraries\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Automating test cases or mocks\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Simple codemods\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"learn-these-terms\" tabindex=\"-1\">\u003ca class=\"anchor\" href=\"#learn-these-terms\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cspan class=\"anchor-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003c/span>\u003c/a>Learn these terms\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abstract_syntax_tree\">\u003cstrong>AST\u003c/strong>\u003c/a>: Source code abstracted as a JavaScript object. When Babel parses code, it\ntransforms it into this.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003cstrong>Nodes\u003c/strong>: These are objects representing specific \u003ca href=\"https://babeljs.io/docs/en/babel-types\">Babel types\u003c/a>\nin the AST\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003cstrong>Paths\u003c/strong>: These are objects that link nodes to one another in the AST\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Visitor_pattern\">\u003cstrong>Visitor\u003c/strong>\u003c/a>: Visitors\nallow you to perform operations on specific paths in the AST based on\ntheir type\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"treat-yourself\" tabindex=\"-1\">\u003ca class=\"anchor\" href=\"#treat-yourself\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cspan class=\"anchor-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003c/span>\u003c/a>Treat yourself\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Do yourself a favor and prefer TypeScript to JavaScript when writing your plugin.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Type guards (e.g. \u003ccode>t.isObjectProperty(path)\u003c/code>) in \u003ccode>@babel/types\u003c/code> create a flawless autocomplete\nexperience and result in more resilient plugins.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"libraries-you'll-need\" tabindex=\"-1\">\u003ca class=\"anchor\" href=\"#libraries-you'll-need\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cspan class=\"anchor-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003c/span>\u003c/a>Libraries you'll need\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@babel/core\">\u003cstrong>@babel/core\u003c/strong>\u003c/a>: Parse source code into an AST and transform it.\nIn particular, see the \u003ccode>parseAsync()\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>transformAsync()\u003c/code> API references.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@babel/types\">\u003cstrong>@babel/types\u003c/strong>\u003c/a>: Check node types and construct new AST nodes.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@babel/generator\">\u003cstrong>@babel/generator\u003c/strong>\u003c/a>: Generate source code from an AST.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@babel/template\">\u003cstrong>@babel/template\u003c/strong>\u003c/a>: Build an AST from strings and placeholders\nrather than the utility functions in \u003ccode>@babel/types\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://babeljs.io/docs/en/next/babel-helper-plugin-utils.html\">\u003cstrong>@babel/helper-plugin-utils\u003c/strong>\u003c/a>: Provide clear messages\nto your plugin users if their Babel version doesn't have APIs required by your plugin.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/babel-utils/babel-plugin-tester\">\u003cstrong>babel-plugin-tester\u003c/strong>\u003c/a>: The easiest way to test your babel plugin.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"resources\" tabindex=\"-1\">\u003ca class=\"anchor\" href=\"#resources\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cspan class=\"anchor-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003c/span>\u003c/a>Resources\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/kentcdodds/babel-plugin-handbook/blob/master/README.md#table-of-contents\">\u003cstrong>Babel Plugin Handbook\u003c/strong>\u003c/a>: Go\ndeeper into Babel plugin concepts.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://babeljs.io/docs/en/babel-types\">\u003cstrong>Babel Types\u003c/strong>\u003c/a>: Quickly search for the AST\nnode types you're looking for.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/kentcdodds/babel-plugin-macros\">\u003cstrong>Babel Plugin Macros\u003c/strong>\u003c/a>: Allow\nplugin users to utilize your plugin transformations without adding it to their\nBabel config. This is useful for libraries like \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/facebook/create-react-app\">create-react-app\u003c/a>\nthat don't allow you to customize your plugins.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"finding-examples\" tabindex=\"-1\">\u003ca class=\"anchor\" href=\"#finding-examples\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cspan class=\"anchor-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003c/span>\u003c/a>Finding examples\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003cstrong>Hiding in plain sight\u003c/strong>: The best place to find example plugins is the \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/babel/babel/tree/eea156b2cb8deecfcf82d52aa1b71ba4995c7d68/packages\">Babel monorepo\u003c/a>\nitself.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003cstrong>Less is more\u003c/strong>: The more basic the plugin, the more fruitful for understanding.\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/babel/babel/blob/eea156b2cb8deecfcf82d52aa1b71ba4995c7d68/packages/babel-plugin-proposal-export-default-from/src/index.js\">@babel/plugin-proposal-export-default-from\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/babel/babel/blob/eea156b2cb8deecfcf82d52aa1b71ba4995c7d68/packages/babel-plugin-transform-react-constant-elements/src/index.js\">@babel/plugin-transform-react-constant-elements\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/babel/babel/blob/eea156b2cb8deecfcf82d52aa1b71ba4995c7d68/packages/babel-plugin-transform-object-assign/src/index.js\">@babel/plugin-transform-object-assign\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/babel/babel/blob/eea156b2cb8deecfcf82d52aa1b71ba4995c7d68/packages/babel-plugin-transform-duplicate-keys/src/index.js\">@babel/plugin-transform-duplicate-keys\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"anatomy-of-a-plugin\" tabindex=\"-1\">\u003ca class=\"anchor\" href=\"#anatomy-of-a-plugin\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cspan class=\"anchor-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003c/span>\u003c/a>Anatomy of a plugin\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>This is a contrived example of a Babel plugin that hoists all duplicate \u003ccode>StringLiteral\u003c/code> types to\na higher scope. In the real world more nuanced logic is required to avoid replacing object\nproperty keys and mutable strings willy-nilly.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003cstrong>What you're going to see\u003c/strong>\u003c/p>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Plugin options, state\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>A few built-in plugin utilities\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>What \u003ccode>enter()\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>exit()\u003c/code> visitors look like\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-ts\">\u003cfigure class=\"code-block\" style=\"background-color:#121212;color:#dbd7caee\">\u003cfigcaption class=\"code-block-title\">src/utils.ts\u003c/figcaption>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy-button\" data-copy-code=\"\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\">Copy\u003c/button>\u003cpre class=\"shiki vitesse-dark\" style=\"background-color:#121212;color:#dbd7caee\" tabindex=\"0\" title=\"src/utils.ts\">\u003ccode class=\"language-ts\">\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#4D9375\">import\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#CB7676\"> *\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#4D9375\"> as\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#BD976A\"> t\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#4D9375\"> from\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#C98A7D77\"> \"\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#C98A7D\">@babel/types\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#C98A7D77\">\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#4D9375\">import\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#CB7676\"> *\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#4D9375\"> as\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#BD976A\"> babel\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#4D9375\"> from\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#C98A7D77\"> \"\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#C98A7D\">@babel/core\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#C98A7D77\">\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#4D9375\">export\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#4D9375\"> default\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#CB7676\"> function\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#80A665\"> babelPluginHoistCommonStrings\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">()\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\"> {\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#4D9375\">  return\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\"> {\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">    // This provides the user with better error messages if\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">    // our plugin throws\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#B8A965\">    name\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">: \u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#C98A7D77\">\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#C98A7D\">hoist-common-strings\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#C98A7D77\">\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">    // And here is the meat of your plugin - the visitor\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#B8A965\">    visitor\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">: {\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">      /**\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">       * \u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">@\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#4D9375\">param\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#BD976A\"> path\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\"> This is the Path we talked about above. It\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">       *  is an object that links Nodes together.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">       * \u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">@\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#4D9375\">param\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#BD976A\"> state\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\"> An object that contains a bunch of metadata\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">       *  about the ... state ... of the transformation. Here you'll find:\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">       *    - state.ast: The current AST from its root Node\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">       *    - state.code: The code string being transformed\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">       *    - state.opts: Plugin options\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">       *    - state.cwd: The working directory of the user\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">       *    - state.filename: The absolute filename of file\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">       *      currently being transformed\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">       */\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#80A665\">      StringLiteral\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#BD976A\">path\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">: \u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#5DA994\">babel\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#5DA994\">NodePath\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">&#x3C;\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#5DA994\">t\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#5DA994\">StringLiteral\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">>, \u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#BD976A\">state\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">: \u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#5DA994\">any\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">) {\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">        // state.opts give us access to options specific to this plugin\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">        // provided by the user with ['hoist-common-strings', {...options...}]\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#CB7676\">        const \u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#BD976A\"> minLen\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\"> =\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#4C9A91\"> 2\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\"> }\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\"> =\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#BD976A\"> state\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#BD976A\">opts\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">        // Here we're going to add the paths for each string literal that\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">        // was used to our state. This will allow us to count them later\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#758575DD\">        // and make sure our `minUses` option was surpassed.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#CB7676\">        const \u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#BD976A\"> node\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\"> }\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\"> =\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#BD976A\"> path\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\n\u003cspan class=\"line\">\u003cspan style=\"color:#BD976A\">        state\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#BD976A\">commonStrings\u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#666666\"> = \u003c/span>\u003cspan style=\"color:#BD976A\">state\u003c/s